.TH DEB-FIND-CHANGES 1 "November 2026" "deb-find-changes 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
deb-find-changes \- list orphaned and locally modified files on Debian systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deb-find-changes
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deb-find-changes
walks the given directory trees (typically
.IR /etc )
and prints, one absolute path per line, the files that dpkg does not
fully account for, so that a backup tool such as
.B extract
can save just those files.
.PP
Two kinds of file are reported.
An
.B orphan
is a regular file (or a symlink to one) that is not owned by any
installed package and is not in the ucf registry.
A
.B modified
file is owned by a package, or registered with ucf, but fails
verification: its MD5 checksum differs from the one recorded in
.I /var/lib/dpkg/info/*.md5sums
or in the
.B Conffiles
field of
.IR /var/lib/dpkg/status ,
or from the ucf hash.
Owned files with no checksum available, or that cannot be read, are
also reported as modified.
Conffiles of removed-but-not-purged (rc) packages are still verified.
Directories, dangling symlinks and special files are ignored.
.PP
The dpkg and ucf databases are read directly; no
.BR dpkg (1)
process is run per file.
Results are written to standard output (or to a file with
.BR \-O );
warnings and progress messages go to standard error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-show\-modified
Report only modified files.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-show\-orphans
Report only orphans.
By default both modified files and orphans are reported.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type
Prefix each line with its type: M (modified) or O (orphan), followed by a space.
.TP
.BI \-x ", " \-\-exclude= GLOB
Exclude files matching
.IR GLOB .
May be repeated.
See
.BR EXCLUDES .
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-from= FILE
Read exclude patterns from
.IR FILE ,
one per line.
May be repeated.
A missing or unreadable file is a warning, not an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-package= PKG
Exclude all files owned by package
.IR PKG .
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-O ", " \-\-output= FILE
Write the list atomically to
.I FILE
(mode 0600) instead of standard output.
On failure any previous
.I FILE
is left untouched.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity.
.B \-v
logs progress per package and tree;
.B \-vv
also logs per-file decisions, including checksum mismatches.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-warnings ", " \-\-no\-warnings
Emit (default) or suppress warnings.
.TP
.BI \-\-admindir= DIR
dpkg administrative directory (default
.IR /var/lib/dpkg ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ucf\-dir= DIR
ucf state directory (default
.IR /var/lib/ucf ).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.PP
Each
.I path
must be an existing directory; relative paths are made absolute.
.SH EXCLUDES
Patterns come from
.BR \-\-exclude ,
.BR \-\-exclude\-from
files and
.BR \-\-exclude\-package .
In an exclude file, blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored, and a line of the form
.BI @ package
excludes that package (its files are neither verified nor reported).
.PP
Pattern forms:
.TP
No \fB/\fR
Glob matched against the basename, e.g.
.IR "*~" ,
.IR "core*" ,
.IR ".*.sw?" .
.TP
Starts with \fB/\fR
Glob matched against the full path, or any leading path prefix ending at a
.B /
boundary, so a directory excludes its subtree, e.g.
.IR /etc/alternatives ,
.IR "/etc/rc*.d" .
.TP
Trailing \fB/\fR
Directory name anywhere in the path, e.g.
.IR .git/ .
.TP
Other, containing \fB/\fR
Glob matched against any
.BR / -aligned
suffix of the path, e.g.
.IR "ssl/private/*" .
.PP
Glob metacharacters are
.B *
(any run of characters, including
.BR / ),
.B ?
(one character) and
.BR [...] .
A pattern that fails to compile is a usage error.
.PP
The following are always excluded:
.IR *.dpkg\-dist ,
.IR *.dpkg\-old ,
.IR *.dpkg\-new ,
.IR *.dpkg\-tmp ,
.IR *.dpkg\-bak ,
.IR *.ucf\-dist ,
.IR *.ucf\-old ,
.IR *.ucf\-new .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/deb-find-changes/exclude-etc
Default exclude file (a conffile).
It ends with a commented-out block of patterns for private keys and
credentials; uncomment lines to keep them out of the backup.
.TP
.I /etc/cron.d/deb-find-changes
Runs nightly at midnight:
.B deb-find-changes \-\-no\-warnings \-\-exclude\-from=/etc/deb-find-changes/exclude-etc \-O /var/cache/deb-find-changes/etc.txt /etc
.TP
.I /var/cache/deb-find-changes/etc.txt
The resulting list, read by
.BR extract .
It is also created when the package is first installed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (warnings do not change this).
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure, e.g. the dpkg admin directory is unreadable or the output
file cannot be written.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dpkg (1),
.BR debsums (1),
.BR extract
